<reference id="bacnetAws-LocalBacnetAwsDevice" xml:lang="en" class="- topic/topic       reference/reference "><title class="- topic/title ">Local Device</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc "> This frozen container under a BACnet network represents
a BACnet station on the BACnet internetwork. Its child <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Bacnet Export Table</uicontrol> container provides server-side functions
to export station objects as BACnet objects and service BACnet client
requests. In general, this means that it provides BACnet server responses
to remote client requests from other BACnet devices on a connected
network.</shortdesc><prolog class="- topic/prolog "><metadata class="- topic/metadata "><keywords class="- topic/keywords "><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">local bacnet AWS device</indexterm></keywords></metadata></prolog><refbody class="- topic/body        reference/refbody "><section class="- topic/section "><fig class="- topic/fig "><title class="- topic/title ">Local Device properties</title><image placement="break" scale="65" width="700" href="../graphic/AwsLocalDevice_0000083849.png" class="- topic/image "/></fig><p class="- topic/p ">To access these properties, expand <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Drivers</uicontrol> and the BACnet network, then double-click <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Local Device</uicontrol>.</p><p class="- topic/p ">The Local Bacnet Aws Device has all the same properties and
components of a regular BACnet Local Device.</p><p class="- topic/p ">In addition to
the common properties (Status and Fault Cause), this component has
